Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their potential usage, and important filtering conditions:

• orders.orderid : join key to order_details to locate each order’s line items  
• orders.customerid : identifies which customer placed each order  
• orders.orderdate : filter to the 1998 calendar year → WHERE strftime('%Y', orderdate) = '1998'  
• order_details.unitprice : price of each product line (needed for spend calculation)  
• order_details.quantity : multiply by unitprice to get line total  
• order_details.discount : ignored (spending is calculated “excluding any discounts”)  
• customergroupthreshold.rangebottom / rangetop : numeric bands that define “Low”, “Medium”, “High” spending groups  
• customergroupthreshold.groupname : label of each spending group  

Ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries
(Note: every SELECT is limited to 20 rows where practical so you can inspect results quickly.)

```sql
-- 1. Distinct order years to verify that 1998 data exist
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS order_year
FROM orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. A sample of orders that were placed in 1998
SELECT orderid, customerid, orderdate
FROM orders
WHERE strftime('%Y', orderdate) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. List of unique customers who ordered in 1998
SELECT DISTINCT customerid
FROM orders
WHERE strftime('%Y', orderdate) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Order‑detail rows belonging to 1998 orders (to inspect prices / quantities / discounts)
SELECT od.orderid,
       od.productid,
       od.unitprice,
       od.quantity,
       od.discount
FROM order_details AS od
JOIN orders AS o ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Compute extended price (unitprice × quantity) for each 1998 order line
SELECT od.orderid,
       (od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS line_total
FROM order_details AS od
JOIN orders AS o ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Summarise to an order‑level total (still limited to 1998)
SELECT od.orderid,
       SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS order_total
FROM order_details AS od
JOIN orders AS o ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
GROUP BY od.orderid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Summarise to a customer‑level total spend for 1998
SELECT o.customerid,
       SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
FROM orders AS o
JOIN order_details AS od ON o.orderid = od.orderid
WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
GROUP BY o.customerid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Inspect the customer‑group threshold table
SELECT *
FROM customergroupthreshold
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Attach each 1998 customer to the correct spending group using the thresholds
SELECT ct.groupname,
       c_tot.customerid,
       c_tot.customer_total
FROM (
        SELECT o.customerid,
               SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
        FROM orders AS o
        JOIN order_details AS od ON o.orderid = od.orderid
        WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
        GROUP BY o.customerid
     ) AS c_tot
JOIN customergroupthreshold AS ct
  ON c_tot.customer_total BETWEEN ct.rangebottom AND ct.rangetop
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: number of customers and percentage share per spending group for 1998
SELECT ct.groupname,
       COUNT(*)                               AS customer_count,
       ROUND(
           COUNT(*) * 100.0 /
           (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT customerid)
            FROM orders
            WHERE strftime('%Y', orderdate) = '1998'), 2
       )                                       AS percentage_of_1998_customers
FROM (
        SELECT o.customerid,
               SUM(od.unitprice * od.quantity) AS customer_total
        FROM orders AS o
        JOIN order_details AS od ON o.orderid = od.orderid
        WHERE strftime('%Y', o.orderdate) = '1998'
        GROUP BY o.customerid
     ) AS c_tot
JOIN customergroupthreshold AS ct
  ON c_tot.customer_total BETWEEN ct.rangebottom AND ct.rangetop
GROUP BY ct.groupname
ORDER BY ct.groupname;
```

